### Pre-existing integration-branch repair required to make the gate runnable (documented per Honesty Covenant #9)
This auto-integration branch HEAD did not build before this change, for reasons unrelated to the surface:
apps/windows/TeslaSync.App.Tests/TeslaSync.App.Tests.csproj was corrupt again — multiple concatenated <Project>
roots (the build failed at XML load with MSB4025 "An XML comment cannot contain '--'" at line 10, a nested <!--
inside an already-open comment). The file held 6 </Project> closers, duplicated PropertyGroup / PackageReference
/ ProjectReference / Content groups, and 825 <Compile> lines for only 424 distinct linked sources (~2x
duplication from repeated bad integration merges). Repaired in place exactly as feature-views 0078 / 0093 did
before later merges re-introduced the corruption: collapsed to ONE valid <Project> root holding the
deduplicated UNION of all distinct <Compile> links (424, each verified present on disk -> 0 stale), the single
PropertyGroup, the 3 PackageReferences, the 2 ProjectReferences and the 3 distinct Content fixtures, normalized
to LF, and added the new LifetimeSummary links. No test coverage dropped — 9287 headless tests pass (vs 8739 at
the 0093 baseline; the count grew as surfaces landed since). New distinct <Compile> count after repair: 427
(424 + LifetimeSummary.Model/.Source/.ViewModel.cs).

### Surface deliverable (feature-views/LifetimeSummary/)
LifetimeSummary.Model.cs / .Source.cs / .ViewModel.cs / .cs + Tests/FeatureViews/LifetimeSummaryTests.cs (26
test cases). Parity port of web LifetimeSummary.tsx: a cyan-glow GlassPanel headed by a trending-up icon +
"Lifetime Summary" title, wrapping a responsive 2/3-column grid of the seven lifetime metric tiles (Total
Spent / Total Energy / Total Sessions / Avg Session Cost / Avg Energy per Session / Avg Duration / Free
Sessions). The figures reproduce the web Cost-Analysis page coreStats + lifetimeMetrics memos verbatim: total
cost = Σ cost_decimal (?? 0); total energy = convertEnergyFromSI(Σ total_energy_added_wh, kWh) = Σwh/1000; total
duration = Σ per-session whole minutes; the lifetime averages = count>0 ? total/count : 0; free sessions = the
sessions whose cost is absent/zero, and free energy keeps the RAW Σ total_energy_added_wh (Wh) yet is labeled
"kWh" — the web's own quirk, reproduced exactly (a unit-test asserts "2 (10,000.0 kWh)" so the parity is
pinned, not silently "fixed"). Currency = formatCurrency(…, 2); energy = fmtWithUnit(…, 'kWh', 1); counts =
fmtInt; duration = `${fmtNumber(…,0)} min`. Full native state matrix: loading (per-metric skeletons) / loaded
(the seven tiles) / empty (the web "No data" surface when no sessions back the figures) / error (retry surface)
/ stale (stale chip) / offline (offline chip + cached tiles). Data via GET /charging-sessions through the shared
cache-then-network engine (no HTTP in the view). Narrator names on every tile and interactive element; the
trend icon is marked decorative (AccessibilityView.Raw); the loading grid is a polite live region;
view.opened slug=LifetimeSummary emitted once on open (PII-safe — no cost/energy/count in diagnostics).

